{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Good Deeds"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Volunteering"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 13}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange information about unlikely events or fairly certain conditions that will be fulfilled in present, past or future  in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Must for Personal Obligation"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use and hear the modal <span class=\"strong\">must</span> in many contexts. When you want to refer to an obligation that you put on yourself, you can use <span class=\"strong\">must</span> rather than <span class=\"strong\">have to</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you oblige yourself to do something, it means that you impose a certain duty on yourself for some reason. When you want to communicate that idea, you can use <span class=\"strong\">must</span>. You use have to when the obligation is imposed upon you from an outside authority."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">must</span> remember to make that dentist appointment - I keep forgetting! <br/>I <span class=\"strong\">must</span> buy my sister a birthday present - her birthday is next week! <br/>We <span class=\"strong\">have to</span> wear a uniform at work. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I <span class=\"italic\">must</span> stay healthy."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I <span class=\"italic\">have to</span> do more to support my community."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I <span class=\"italic\">must</span> get more practical work experience."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I <span class=\"italic\">must</span> be more social."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I <span class=\"italic\">must</span> work on my personal development."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "First Conditional: Modal Verbs Will, May, and Might "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the<span class=\"strong\"> first conditional</span> to talk about real or possible situations."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use the modal verb will in the result clause, you communicate the fact that the result is quite possible or even certain."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure of the <span class=\"strong\">  first conditional </span>is usually<br />  If+present simple (If clause) and will +infinitive (result clause). <br /><br /> Remember to use a comma (,) if the If clause is at the beginning of the sentence.  <br />For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">If I don't study for the test, <span class=\"strong\">I won't pass</span>. </span> <br /> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">I won't pass </span>if I don't study for the test. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can choose to use <span class=\"strong\">may</span> or <span class=\"strong\">might</span> instead of <span class=\"strong\">will</span> when you want to talk about a result that is less certain. It is possible, but not definite."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">If it snows tomorrow, <span class=\"strong\">I may stay home or I might go to the mall</span>. I don't know yet. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "In the<span class=\"strong\"> first conditional</span>, there is no difference in meaning between <span class=\"italic\">may</span> and <span class=\"italic\">might</span>. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you become a volunteer, you may achieve many of them. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Experts report that if you focus on something or someone other than yourself, your outlook will change, which may alter some stress-producing mechanisms in the body. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you donate your time, local hospitals and community centers will be able to invest their precious resources in other areas."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you volunteer for a non-profit organization, you might learn about the operations of government."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you understand community needs, you may develop empathy and feelings of self-efficacy. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "primarily "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "mainly; mostly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Volunteering provides physical and mental rewards, primarily by reducing stress."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le13ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about moral and personal dilemmas."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mechanism "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a process or procedure"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Experts report that if you focus on something or someone other than yourself, your outlook will change, which may alter some stress-producing mechanisms in the body. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le13ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fate "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "destiny; what will happen in the future"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Volunteering also makes you healthier in other ways. Feelings like optimism, joy, and control over one's fate are known to strengthen the immune system."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le13ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to donate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to give"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you donate your time, local hospitals and community centers will be able to invest in other things. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le13ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "resources "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "money or other things required to do something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Local institutions have limited resources to fulfill their mission."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le13ob05aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "non-profit organization"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "similar to a private company but with the overall goal of helping people instead of making money"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: For example, if you volunteer for a non-profit organization, you might learn about the operations of government."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le13ob05aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss what volunteers do at those places."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find more information about volunteer work opportunities online or in other ways, such as at a c